Photosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria convert sunlight into chemical energy. In the chloroplasts, chlorophyll absorbs sunlight and uses that energy to split water molecules into oxygen, protons, and electrons. The released electrons help convert carbon dioxide into glucose through a series of reactions, with oxygen being released as a byproduct.
